## Audio credits

Every sound in assets/ is baked into the binary at compile time, so it
travels with any copy of this crate. Each file carries its own licence —
two of them are CC-BY, where credit is a legal condition of redistribution
and not a courtesy. Do not collapse these into one blanket line.

All files were transcoded to Ogg Vorbis for the build. Any further change
is recorded per file.

  assets/ambience.ogg
    "Dark horror ambience" by LukaCafuka — CC0 1.0
    https://freesound.org/people/LukaCafuka/sounds/758478/
    Modified: body re-cut as a seamless loop with a crossfade at the
    seam, and transcoded from WAV to Ogg Vorbis.

  assets/laugh.ogg
    "Evil Laugh 1" by prometheus_crr — CC0 1.0
    https://freesound.org/people/prometheus_crr/sounds/593305/

  assets/jump_scare.ogg
    "Piano Scare" by ERT3001 — CC0 1.0
    https://freesound.org/people/ERT3001/sounds/723292/

  assets/scream.ogg
    "Woman Screaming" by DanJFilms — CC0 1.0
    https://freesound.org/people/DanJFilms/sounds/845164/

  assets/thunder.ogg
    "rock_breaking" (from Yo Frankie!) by Blender Foundation
    CC-BY 3.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
    Source: https://opengameart.org/content/rockbreaking
    Modified: transcoded from FLAC to Ogg Vorbis.

  assets/incantation_1.ogg, assets/incantation_2.ogg
    "Creepy Latin Speech 3 Prayer or Summoning Deep Voice"
    by DeqstersLab — CC-BY 4.0
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Source: https://freesound.org/people/DeqstersLab/sounds/807452/
    Modified: split into two excerpts, converted to mono, faded,
    loudness-normalised, and transcoded from MP3 to Ogg Vorbis.

  assets/bell.ogg
    "120122_church_bells_Minoritenkirche.wav" by reinsamba
    CC-BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Source: https://freesound.org/people/reinsamba/sounds/143964/
    Modified: excerpted, converted to mono, high-pass filtered, faded,
    loudness-normalised, and transcoded to Ogg Vorbis.


CC-BY requires four things for each work: the author, the title, the
licence with a link, and a statement that changes were made. The transcode
alone is a change, so every "Modified:" line above is a requirement rather
than a note.
